---
description: |
  Summarizes HarfangLab network connection documents (`event.category`
  `network`) into one document per window, host, process executable and
  user, local and remote IP address, destination domain, service port,
  transport, and direction. Other documents, including `network_listen`
  documents, pass through unchanged.

  Each summary stays an ECS network document. `event.start` and `event.end`
  hold the times of the first and last connection, `event.duration` the time
  between them in nanoseconds, and `@timestamp` equals `event.start`. ECS has
  no field for the number of events that a document stands for, so
  `tenzir.count` holds the number of connections.

  HarfangLab's ECS documents name the connecting side in `source` and the
  accepting side in `destination`, so the service port is
  `destination.port` in both directions. The remote end is `source` for
  inbound connections (`network.direction` `in`) and `destination`
  otherwise. The client port appears only if all connections of the summary
  had the same one, so the summary of a single connection keeps it. The geo
  record of the remote end comes from the first connection of the summary.

  The summary takes the host, agent, and organization from the first document
  of the host with the same `network` record in the window.

  Windows close on the wall clock every `window`, and every summary covers at
  most one `window` of event time. The package description explains the
  windowing, the memory it needs, and how a SIEM counts summaries.
args:
  named:
    - name: window
      type: duration
      default: 5min
      description: Width of the summary windows, in processing and event time.
---

// `$window` names the argument only outside the `window` block.
if event.category?.first() == "network" {
  _host = host?.id? else agent?.id? else host?.hostname?
  _time = time(this["@timestamp"]?)
  _bucket = _time.floor($window)
  _inbound = network?.direction? == "in"
  _remote_ip = source?.ip? if _inbound else destination?.ip?
  _local_ip = destination?.ip? if _inbound else source?.ip?
  // Every group key and aggregate costs memory per summary. The values in
  // `_ids` are few per host, so the summaries group by their digest and take
  // them from one context record per host and digest. The host, agent, and
  // organization come from the first document of the context.
  _ids = hash_xxh3([host?.id?, host?.hostname?, agent?.id?, agent?.name?,
    event?.kind?, event?.type?, network?, process?.user?.name?])
  window size=$window {
    fork_merge {
      summarize _host, _bucket, _ids, process?.executable?, _remote_ip,
        _local_ip, destination?.domain?, destination?.port?,
        count=count(), start=min(_time), end=max(_time),
        _remote_geo=first(source?.geo? if _inbound else destination?.geo?),
        _client_port_min=min(source?.port?), _client_port_max=max(source?.port?),
        _client_port_count=count(source?.port?)
    }, {
      summarize _host, _ids, _context=first({
        agent: agent?,
        ecs: ecs?,
        kind: event?.kind?,
        type: event?.type?,
        host: host?,
        network: network?,
        organization: organization?,
        user: process?.user?.name?,
      })
    }
    // The context of a host and digest sorts before its summaries, so a
    // running `first` hands it to each of them.
    sort _host, _ids, _context? == null
    summarize _host, _ids, _ctx=first(_context?),
      options={mode: "cumulative"}
    where _context? == null
    _inbound = _ctx.network?.direction? == "in"
    _client_port = (_client_port_min
      if _client_port_min == _client_port_max
        and _client_port_count == count else null)
    this = {
      "@timestamp": start,
      agent: _ctx.agent,
      destination: {
        ip: _local_ip if _inbound else _remote_ip,
        geo: null if _inbound else _remote_geo,
        domain: destination.domain,
        port: destination.port,
      },
      ecs: _ctx.ecs,
      event: {
        category: ["network"],
        kind: _ctx.kind,
        type: _ctx.type,
        start: start,
        end: end,
        duration: int((end - start) / 1ns),
      },
      host: _ctx.host,
      network: _ctx.network,
      organization: _ctx.organization,
      process: {
        executable: process.executable,
        user: {name: _ctx.user} if _ctx.user != null else null,
      },
      source: {
        ip: _remote_ip if _inbound else _local_ip,
        geo: _remote_geo if _inbound else null,
        port: _client_port,
      },
      tenzir: {count: count},
    }
    drop_null_fields
  }
}
